  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to: (1) identify small probability outcomes (here, 1% in B), (2) increase their weight by 10 percentage points (to 11%), and (3) compute a weighted sum of outcomes using these adjusted probabilities and compare it to the weighted sum of A. The individual does not apply the 10 percentage point adjustment; instead, they dismiss the 1% outcome as 'unlikely to occur' without any formal weighting adjustment. The justification is based on a belief in the impossibility of the outcome, not on a rule-based weighting. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason as specified. The reasoning is qualitatively different — it reflects a belief in the rarity of the outcome rather than a formal probabilistic adjustment. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
